<title>JAPAN: JSAT to launch fifth satellite next year.</title>
<headline>JSAT to launch fifth satellite next year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Satellite Systems Inc (JSAT) announced on Tuesday that it would launch its fifth communications satellite, the JCSAT-5, in November 1997.</p>
<p>The satellite, made by Hughes Space and Communications International, a unit of General Motors Corp, will be launched from a Martin Marietta Commercial Launch Services rocket, JSAT said.</p>
<p>JSAT is owned by Itochu Corp, Mitsui &amp; Co, Sumitomo Corp and Nissho Iwai Corp.</p>
<p>The new satellite will cover all of Asia, including Japan, and Hawaii, JSAT said.</p>
</text>
